  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PhosAgro/UNESCO/IUPAC Partnership in Green Chemistry for Life</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In essence, the Project&apos;s activities cover the launching and implementation over five years of an international research grants programme for innovative one-year research projects in green chemistry and/or the use of its advances. Green chemistry is currently very much in the spotlight since it is a novel area of chemistry developed during the last two decades, and it brings a new approach for the protection of the environment, human health and the quality of life, and represents a significant departure from the traditional methods previously used.</narrative>
  </description>
